Description: Stereo 3D: one output, both eyes as complete pictures side by side, declared to Stereo KWin
 Dolphin's own Depth, Convergence, per-game Depth Percentage, Convergence and
 Monoscopic Shadows, their hotkeys and defaults stay upstream's. The other
 stereo output modes (top and bottom, anaglyph, quad buffer, passive), the eye
 swap and the half-width eyes are not built: Stereo KWin's outputs make every
 format, and the eye swap is the output's. OpenGL draws the two eyes into a
 window the desktop makes two views wide (libstereo-declare); Vulkan renders
 each eye into its own image layer, which the graphics driver packs and
 declares. The interface and the on-screen messages are drawn in both eyes, at
 the screen. 3D is on by default; a desktop without the pair shows 2D and says
 nothing unless the person turned 3D on; a renderer or surface that cannot give
 two views is told. The no-GUI front end shows 2D and says so.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Origin: vendor, Sparky Stereo OS (ORDER 39), branch order39 of the edition's fork
Last-Update: 2026-11-19

